<title>INDIA: Indian cotton prices ease on sluggish mill buying.</title>
<headline>Indian cotton prices ease on sluggish mill buying.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian cotton prices eased on Friday on sluggish mill buying and higher new crop supplies, dealers said.</p>
<p>Volumes were thin as major players kept sidelines awaiting the outcome of a meeting of Cotton Advisory Board on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Indian government is likely to release more export of cotton only after this meeting,&quot; one broker added.</p>
<p>--Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
